  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry and seasonably mild early Autumn weather \ncontinue through this weekend and into the last week of October.\n\nPersistent, incredibly low precipitable water values (under 0.4\nof an inch) will continue to reside over all of Central PA today\nand tonight under a ridge of high pressure. \n\nA band of slightly higher PWAT (0.5-0.7 of an inch) and some \nsct-bkn, shallow stratocu (mainly across the Northern Mtns) \nwill advect south through the CWA in the wake of a weak/dry cold\nfront later Thursday morning and Thu afternoon as some limited \nmoisture is picked up off the Lower Glakes. \n\nThe stretch of sensational weather continues into the last week\nof October. This rain-free pattern (Zero POPs areawide through \nMonday) is highlighted by generally sunny and warm afternoons \nwith low humidity followed by clear and chilly moonlit nights \nwith areas of frost and river valley fog. \n\nHigh temps will average anywhere from normal (Susq Valley and\nSouthern PA Valleys to 7 or 8 deg F above normal (Central and NW\nMtns) today and Thursday before taking a brief dip to near or\nslightly below normal in most places on friday. A gradual\nrebound in temps will occur for Sat through Monday, with\nMonday's maxes averaging 8-11 deg f above normal (which equates\nto low-mid 60s across the Northern and Western Mtns and near 70\nin the Southern Valleys).",
